      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing a Provider**\n\nI've decided to move forward with Google Cloud Pub/Sub as the messaging provider for `dead_letter.py`. The plan now is to build the Python code within the file that utilizes the Google Cloud Pub/Sub client to handle these tasks, specifically sending failed messages.\n\n\n**Defining the Core Function**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on the function within `dead_letter.py` that will handle sending messages to the dead-letter topic. The function, tentatively named `send_to_dead_letter`, will accept the message and the dead-letter topic path as inputs. I'll be leveraging the `google.cloud.pubsub_v1.PublisherClient` to publish these messages. I'm taking steps to ensure the code is robust, including considering ways to make it easy to modify the message content for debugging. I'm also including the provider-specific identifiers.\n\n\n",
