      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing Cloud Provider**\n\nI've decided to use Google Cloud Pub/Sub and am getting started on a Python script, `consume_event.py`, that retrieves a single message from a managed subscription. The goal is now to write the script, but I'm focusing on the provider setup.\n\n\n**Defining the Consumption Process**\n\nI'm now creating the Python file, `consume_event.py`, specifically using the Google Cloud Pub/Sub library, `google-cloud-pubsub`. The code will import `pubsub_v1` from `google.cloud` and define a function that consumes a single message. I plan to use `SubscriberClient` to connect to Pub/Sub, specifying a project and subscription ID. I'll call `subscribe` and `pull` (or a similar method) to retrieve and then acknowledge the received message.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789865094498,
          "start": 1789865091563
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
